{%- comment -%}
  Project thumbnail, shared by the index card and the detail header.
  `thumbnail:` is `gradient-1` (blush), `gradient-2` (lavender) or an image path; an
  empty one falls back to `img:` (al-folio's field), then to `gradient-1`.

  include.project  the project document
  include.class    extra class for size (`project-thumb--hero`, `--card`)

  The gradient is whatever the front matter says, on the card and on the detail
  page alike. Alternating it by grid position instead made the two disagree,
  since a detail page has no position. Keeping blush and lavender from
  repeating is therefore done in the content: write them alternating down the
  `importance` order within a category.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign thumb = include.project.thumbnail | default: include.project.img | default: 'gradient-1' -%}
{%- assign thumb_head = thumb | slice: 0, 9 -%}
{%- if thumb_head == 'gradient-' -%}
  <div class="project-thumb project-thumb--{{ thumb }} {{ include.class }}" aria-hidden="true"></div>
{%- else -%}
  <div class="project-thumb project-thumb--image {{ include.class }}" aria-hidden="true">
    <img src="{{ thumb | relative_url }}" alt="" loading="lazy">
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
